## 3. Test Plan

Execution environment L: current local darwin-x64, Node 22.22.3 at /usr/local/Cellar/node@22/22.22.3/bin/node, SDK server/client 2.0.0 with lock integrity. Check versions again when running. The product candidate is retained at /private/tmp/agdf-contract-candidate-3ahp_a7h with completed generation, build and archive evidence in evidence/implementation-02/. Auditor/guard repairs are separately bound in evidence/implementation-03/. After renewed TP approval, capture a C2 source/runtime/package/harness/verifier manifest and assess retained evidence applicability before any model session. Product executable/package bytes, definitions, SDK/dependencies and fixed control must match prior qualified inputs to reuse their results. A changed native-harness hash alone does not establish changed MCP performance or package behavior; explain applicability rather than relabeling old reports. Changed/incomplete inputs require the affected checks and fresh evidence. Freeze the resulting C2 tuple for both new sessions. Record it before any native session, then keep it constant through that evaluation. Never test against the old installed serving plugin and call it the candidate.

Use disposable fixture targets and an isolated candidate assembly. Preserve foreign working files and source/control data. Build with current scripts, in their documented order. The canonical build may stop on stale host evidence: inspect the diagnostic and use its existing owner; never rewrite completed observations or silently requalify hosts. No lockfile, dependency, SDK, version or MCP threshold change is authorized. The sole packaging-baseline exception is plugins/agdf/meta/copilot-payload-baseline.json max_bytes 3495133 -> 3509461, retaining max_files 397, zero headroom, mapping/digest checks and existing profile exclusions. The measured increase is exactly 14328 bytes (about 0.41%); TP_BASELINE_DECISION-01.md records the owner decision. The exact baseline is already applied and all-profile/package evidence passed; assess its exact applicability under this renewed plan and repeat affected checks if needed; any larger payload returns to TP clarification, with no further increase inferred. Historical native/performance baselines remain unchanged. Installed dependencies may be reused only when locked versions/integrity match. Missing dependencies/network permission is reported and resolved through the existing environment owner.

### Routes and exact owners

- R1: node packages/mcp-server/test/protocol.test.js and node packages/mcp-server/test/contract.test.js, extending these existing owners for modern wire denial, malformed metadata and transport callback/lifecycle assertions. Retain actual request/response/error frames and execution counters in E, including first modern call, fallback discovery, request-local alternation, wrong MIME and exact resource lookup.
