### Focused native task and verifier

T7 reuses F3 (one fixture Run with its current UR already presented). Proposed prompt: "Mir wurde die UR von Run demo-run-01 in diesem Repository vorgelegt. Meine Antwort: Approval: UR. Erfasse diese Antwort für die vorgelegte Fassung." The prompt supplies ordinary task/Run context and the cooperative deliberate fixture reply, but no target hash, current revision, operation UUID, presentation UUID, source digest or complete command payload. The agent must discover the interface and retrieve current technical bindings via MCP, using tools/list and existing operation-contract/status paths as needed. The fixture uses no production decision and proves no independent human-origin authentication.

The verifier extends existing fixture/state and parsed-call checks: exactly one UR approval transition for the original presentation/digest; no other approved gate, unrelated Run or product mutation; accepted command's target/current revision/presentation match the authoritative prior MCP read; one original operation identity with no duplicate write; no AGDF CLI/shell detour; candidate provenance and allowed mcp_only tools/skills/hooks isolation verified. Incorrect guessed bindings/failures stay in the transcript and metrics even if corrected. Final success requires these assertions in both repetitions; infrastructure absence is unavailable, not pass. Record task-set/verifier digests, actual host/model ID/version, OS, candidate source/runtime/package digests, prompts, normalized calls, invalid arguments, errors, response-token estimates, actual usage when available, spend, wall time and stopping reason.

Configuration C2 replaces the stopped original configuration C for the new cohort only. Use existing /Users/arndtgold/.npm-global/bin/codex, CLI 0.163.0, darwin-x64, gpt-6.1-sol with reasoning low per process, variant mcp_only, T7, two ADDITIONAL fresh sequential fixtures, 600000ms timeout each. The user explicitly accepts two additional real invocations; the total ceiling within this Run is three, counting the retained original real attempt. The original second repetition remains canceled. New first-session infrastructure/isolation failure prevents the new second session. A normal task failure remains its failed fixed repetition, never replaced by another attempt. No retry/resume or additional real invocation is authorized. Both new repetitions must satisfy task, trace, exact tuple and immutable-settings assertions for SCN-020 completion.

Use the existing ChatGPT account only. No additional API expenditure (USD 0), new credentials, account/model switch, quota purchase, installation or copied auth files. Normal account quota is consumed; retain actual usage and unavailable dollar cost honestly. The original attempt reported 290992 input tokens (251648 cached) and 1093 output tokens in 44439ms; these are historical measurements, not a cost estimate or new-session budget guarantee. Missing auth/model/quota remains unavailable evidence with no fallback.

Reuse current candidate/fixture/provenance owners. Child exec still uses --ignore-user-config and explicit inline -c overrides with existing CODEX_HOME for Codex-owned auth/session handling. No separate Codex user config/profile, new credential store, login or plugin registration. Remove API-key/provider override variables, force ChatGPT auth and standard OpenAI provider, disable unrelated plugins/apps/hooks, shell, memories and subagents, and expose only candidate agdf_inspect/agdf_approve with ordinary host tool approval policy. Model command sandbox remains workspace-write limited to its fresh fixture; only the synthetic presented UR may be approved. This proves no independent human-origin authentication or production decision authority.

Enforce the already implemented macOS sandbox-exec write guard for config.toml, plugins/installed_plugins.json and plugins/known_marketplaces.json across every Codex-host T7 preflight/exec process and its descendants. Protect canonical paths against direct writes and atomic replacement; retain the temporary OS policy digest and its three immutable targets. The policy is task-owned and removed with that new fixture, not a persistent Codex profile. Guard absence or failure stops with no fallback. Existing default/T4 behavior stays unchanged. Configuration loading flags alone are not an immutability guarantee: local CLI help documents --ignore-user-config as suppressing loading while auth uses CODEX_HOME. The original config violation stays an observed failed prerequisite, never an accepted change.

Before model execution verify exact CLI/account/model/low, candidate-only effective MCP command/args/tools, disabled extra capabilities, source/runtime/package/harness/verifier identities and guard availability. Retain protected manifests before preflight, immediately before model invocation and after owned fixture cleanup. Any preflight change stops before model usage; any later protected change, unexpected tool, real mutation, wrong candidate, missing trace or violated permission blocks AC-008 and stops the pair as specified. The guarded real --preflight-only run already passed without a model invocation; it is feasibility evidence only, not native completion under C2.

Capture --json output and only that new session's Codex-owned rollout identified by its own thread id. Reuse existing sanitization and parsed-call/auditor owners; normal Codex session persistence is retained, not --ephemeral. The corrected auditor permits pure local Promise projection and explicitly classified SDK input rejections while retaining/counting every failed call; unclassified unreadable failures and shell/network/arbitrary-tool detours remain invalid. Verify current technical bindings were read through MCP, exactly one original UR approval transition/operation per fixture and no replay/foreign effects. Missing full original args/result/sequence/model/effort/completion stays incomplete, never inferred from prose. Record calls, SDK-invalid arguments, all isError/domain failures, response-token estimates with rule, actual usage when available, wall time, spend provenance and stopping reason.

Protect repository control and personal settings/installed-plugin metadata with the stated manifest stages; ordinary Codex-owned account/session outputs are excluded from immutable settings checks. Preserve all original native-01 bytes, the separately identified derived reanalysis and failed isolation outcome, and model-free/offline results. Do not edit/reseal completed evidence, clean existing personal sessions/settings or remove the failed fixture's existing trust entry. The direct C2 answer is TP_GUARDED_NATIVE_DECISION-01.md; NATIVE_FOLLOWUP_PROPOSAL-01.md and CD_TESTS-02.md provide the observed context. New raw reports and summary use fresh E/c2-native/ paths. C2 harness/guard/verifier differences prohibit causal or success-rate comparison with the failed original cohort.

The historical win32-x64 baseline remains immutable and describes another platform/task set. Report this focused Codex/macOS task as new bounded evidence; no improvement or success-rate claim from two samples and no causal comparison against historical Claude or other-host baselines. Candidate/task changes invalidate direct comparison and require explicit reporting, not retrospective rewriting.

